# Credentials, first and above all. Without this line COPY . . bakes a real
# .env into the image — Anthropic key included — and anyone who can pull that
# image has it. The container receives its configuration through env_file at
# run time, never through a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.recommande

# Rebuilt inside the image by npm ci, and a host tree may hold binaries for
# the wrong platform entirely.
node_modules/
dist/

# Runtime state belongs in the named volume, not in the image. Copying a
# journal in would also mean shipping the operator's trading history.
data/
.tmp/

# Not needed to run, and .git in particular can carry an accidentally
# committed secret in its history long after the file was removed.
.git/
.github/
coverage/
*.log

tests/
docs/
*.md
!README.md
